From e4f34bdce7a21d25b0e876d866cc33ec0efc4e5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wanghan <wanghan58@contributor>


Date: Fri, 13 Feb 2026 11:58:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] BUGFIX Fix crash on truncate table with instant
 drop column when recycle bin enabled

Issue:
Fix the server crash when executing TRUNCATE TABLE on a table that previously had columns dropped using the ALGORITHM=INSTANT method, while the recycle bin is enabled.

Analysis:
The root cause is that when the recycle bin is enabled and a table undergoes a TRUNCATE TABLE operation, it fails to thoroughly purge the metadata for columns dropped using the instant algorithm. This leaves orphaned column metadata residues in the COLUMNS system table.

Solution:
Immediate Workaround:
When the recycle bin is enabled, the TRUNCATE TABLE command is modified to explicitly delete the instant column metadata from the data dictionary. Note that this fix is not yet applicable to partitioned tables.
Long-term Optimization:
The TRUNCATE TABLE workflow will be refactored in the future to ensure cleanup of instant column metadata is performed consistently, regardless of whether the recycle bin is enabled or disabled.
